that you'd like

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:15.940
to add that we have
not mentioned before?

00:22:15.940 --> 00:22:19.520
EMILY MELHUISH: OK, I
have two cool things.

00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:23.580
One cool thing, because with
BigQuery you can basically

00:22:23.580 --> 00:22:28.430
narrow down on really,
really distinct stats

00:22:28.430 --> 00:22:33.310
and data about a certain
view, and so with our tests

00:22:33.310 --> 00:22:36.760
that we run when we're querying
the BigQuery API to check

00:22:36.760 --> 00:22:40.020
the validity of the data,
there was a few times

00:22:40.020 --> 00:22:44.880
when the whole of the data
layer and the custom dimensions

00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:48.540
were null, but there
was still a view logged.

00:22:48.540 --> 00:22:50.820
So it was kind of interesting,
and it was quite fun

00:22:50.820 --> 00:22:53.710
because we got to be all, like,
CSI detective to see, like,

00:22:53.710 --> 00:22:56.340
why is this happening.

00:22:56.340 --> 00:22:57.840
And what we actually
managed to find

00:22:57.840 --> 00:23:00.630
was that there was a
whole bunch of listings

00:23:00.630 --> 00:23:06.540
hit at the exact same timestamp
with the exact same browser ID.

00:23:06.540 --> 00:23:08.520
And they hit all
of these listings.

00:23:08.520 --> 00:23:11.050
And so what we actually
managed to find out

00:23:11.050 --> 00:23:12.930
is that these were
obviously bots,

00:23:12.930 --> 00:23:14.430
like, scraping through the site.

00:23:14.430 --> 00:23:16.850
And they obviously went
through it fast enough

00:23:16.850 --> 00:23:18.650
that the data layer
didn't have time

00:23:18.650 --> 00:23:22.724
to populate and be
sent to GTM properly.

00:23:22.724 --> 00:23:24.015
So that was pretty interesting.

00:23:24.015 --> 00:23:26.310
And I think I was
on Skype with Lester

00:23:26.310 --> 00:23:28.250
being like oh my gosh,
there's these bots, ah!

00:23:28.250 --> 00:23:30.491
And so he was like, oh,
block their browser IDs.

00:23:30.491 --> 00:23:31.490
And it was kind of cool.

00:23:31.490 --> 00:23:33.640
It was a little wee
detective moment

00:23:33.640 --> 00:23:36.760
to sort of be like, oh, bots,
and block them from our data

00:23:36.760 --> 00:23:38.300
so they don't sort
of mess with it.

00:23:38.300 --> 00:23:41.110
So I thought that was pretty
awesome to see that happening

00:23:41.110 --> 00:23:44.535
and then be able to sort of stop
them from affecting our data.

00:23:44.535 --> 00:23:45.410
That was pretty cool.

00:23:45.410 --> 00:23:46.010
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Nice.

