00:25:46.140 --> 00:25:48.110
Like say you're
prototyping or trying

00:25:48.110 --> 00:25:50.840
something out, maybe a proof of
concept, something like that.

00:25:50.840 --> 00:25:52.540
You don't want to have
it running all the time.

00:25:52.540 --> 00:25:54.456
Now, one of the tradeoffs
with App Engine Flex

00:25:54.456 --> 00:25:56.460
is you get a lot
more flexibility,

00:25:56.460 --> 00:25:59.250
you can do whatever you want,
but it doesn't scale to zero.

00:25:59.250 --> 00:26:00.167
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah.

00:26:00.167 --> 00:26:02.125
MARK MANDEL: So you might
want to shut it down.

00:26:02.125 --> 00:26:04.094
Now previously, this
was kind of tricky.

00:26:04.094 --> 00:26:06.010
You had to kind of jump
through some loopholes

00:26:06.010 --> 00:26:08.854
and do some fun things,
and it wasn't great.

00:26:08.854 --> 00:26:11.020
The great thing is now
there's a simple command that

00:26:11.020 --> 00:26:12.014
allows you to do it.

00:26:12.014 --> 00:26:12.930
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Nice.

00:26:12.930 --> 00:26:14.330
And what is the command?

00:26:14.330 --> 00:26:16.944
MARK MANDEL: So it's a
version-specific command.

00:26:16.944 --> 00:26:19.360
So you're like, hey, I want
you to shut down this version.

00:26:19.360 --> 00:26:19.940
FRANCESC CAMPOY: OK.

00:26:19.940 --> 00:26:21.856
MARK MANDEL: So you can
say GCloud preview app

00:26:21.856 --> 00:26:23.920
version stop, and
then the version

00:26:23.920 --> 00:26:25.330
name you want to shut down.

00:26:25.330 --> 00:26:25.780
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Nice.

00:26:25.780 --> 00:26:26.380
It sounds simple.

00:26:26.380 --> 00:26:26.970
MARK MANDEL: It's pretty simple.

00:26:26.970 --> 00:26:28.900
So you can kind of work on
something for a few hours,

00:26:28.900 --> 00:26:29.580
or your day.

00:26:29.580 --> 00:26:31.610
And then once you're done at the
end of the day, shut it down.

00:26:31.610 --> 00:26:33.420
Then you don't have to
worry about paying for it.

00:26:33.420 --> 00:26:34.545
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Very cool.

00:26:34.545 --> 00:26:36.360
That sounds, like,
